      "dcDescription": [
        "1934.06.0002 Collected at Oraibi in 1930. 10.506 Oraibi, SV USA [[Haga]] skiss bild nr 17.987 Hopi konservering k82: 235 Amerika United States Hopi Korg.  Gåva.\nWicker tray basket from Oraibi (Hopi). The design is the so-called whirlwind which refers to the dust whirls which are common in this portion of the Southwest. The warp ribs Are mad eof sumac or willow twigs, the weft of rabbit \nbrush, the edge is wrapped with yucca. The dyes are all native. The Hopis  have perhaps the widest range of native basket dyes in the Southwest.\n\nkonservering k82: 235 Sydvästra USA, Oraibi Årsberättelse 1934, "
