      "dcDescription": [
        "1934.06.0003 Collected at Oraibi in 1930. 10.503 Oraibi, SV USA [[Haga]] skiss bild nr 17.984 Hopi Amerika United States Hopi Korg.  Gåva.\nHopi coiled basket plaque from second Mesa. The design represents a Katcina mask. These baskets are primarily used for decoration, being hung on the walls of the houses, although they also serve as trays. The coil \nfoundation and wrapping are made of yucca, which gives a soft surface in contrast to the other baskets. The dyes are native. Sydvästra USA, Oraibi Årsberättelse 1934, Göteborgs museum, Årstryck 1935"
